;; Operational scratch continuation: StateAddressScatter writes at the current
;; next pointer before incrementing it, and folds those steps in input order.
;; Count-loop pointer refinement plus collision freedom proves every occurrence
;; survives all later writes. Computed write destinations are distinct, bounded
;; and a permutation of scratch positions. Final readback is therefore an input
;; permutation with multiplicities, independent of initial cell contents, and
;; has ascending bucket keys. No permutation/ordering certificate is supplied.
;; Five mutations fail pointer, write-value/destination, untouched-cell or
;; readback-order proofs. Build/env-linter pass; independent review finds no
